WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.272 --> 00:00:02.939
(ambient music)

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.094
- There's more to sight

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:08.513
than just being able to see the crowd.

00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:11.993
You can definitely feel the atmosphere.

00:00:11.993 --> 00:00:13.078
There's a vibe in the air,

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:14.065
there's the energy in the air,

00:00:14.065 --> 00:00:15.721
there's a sound.

00:00:15.721 --> 00:00:18.614
It's amazing to hear the fans,

00:00:18.614 --> 00:00:21.274
especially when we run outta the tunnel.

00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:24.024
(exciting music)

00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:29.911
I'm Jake Olson; I'm the long snapper

00:00:29.911 --> 00:00:32.320
of the University of
Southern California Trojans.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.862
I'm completely blind, I have no eyes.

00:00:35.862 --> 00:00:38.262
I went in to play football
with the mentality

00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:40.859
that I had nothing to lose.

00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:43.102
Long snapping is an art.

00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:44.917
You definitely have the mechanics,

00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:46.658
but a lot of it is just feel.

00:00:46.658 --> 00:00:49.077
Feeling that ball come off
your fingertips in a spiral,

00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:51.079
how hard you're throwing it, you know,
where you're releasing it,

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:52.603
just kinda getting that velocity,

00:00:52.603 --> 00:00:54.103
and that accuracy.

00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:58.647
Life's unfair, football's unfair,

00:00:58.647 --> 00:01:00.527
but at the same time,

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:04.694
it's up to you of how far
you wanna take yourself.

00:01:06.378 --> 00:01:08.442
When I was eight months
old, I was diagnosed

00:01:08.442 --> 00:01:12.897
with a rare form of eye
cancer called retinoblastoma.

00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:15.725
When the doctor found my cancer,

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:17.266
it was completely taking over my left eye,

00:01:17.266 --> 00:01:20.614
so they almost immediately
removed my left eye.

00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:22.504
From there on, you know, just a cycle of,

00:01:22.504 --> 00:01:23.535
you know, the cancer coming back,

00:01:23.535 --> 00:01:25.833
then we fight it with treatments.

00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:27.573
Doctors finally said, listen,

00:01:27.573 --> 00:01:30.190
we've pretty much exhausted
all our treatment options.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.899
The safer option is just, you
know, the removal of the eye.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:38.382
Growing up in the 2000s where
Coach Carroll was so dominant

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:41.882
with USC, it was hard not to be a USC fan.

00:01:43.154 --> 00:01:44.486
I always loved football.

00:01:44.486 --> 00:01:46.630
I continued to play flag
football my eighth grade year,

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.066
after losing my sight.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:52.054
It was not anything
close to tackle football.

00:01:52.054 --> 00:01:54.916
As I entered high school, I
decided not to play football

00:01:54.916 --> 00:01:56.714
for my freshman and sophomore year.

00:01:56.714 --> 00:01:59.905
It really was something that
I didn't think I could do.

00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:01.208
But eventually, my love

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.251
for the game really overcame any doubts,

00:02:03.251 --> 00:02:06.001
and I learned how to be an asset.

00:02:09.344 --> 00:02:11.357
I just love the camaraderie of football;

00:02:11.357 --> 00:02:12.346
I love being part of the team’

00:02:12.346 --> 00:02:13.644
love putting on, you know, just the pads

00:02:13.644 --> 00:02:15.354
and the jersey and stuff,

00:02:15.354 --> 00:02:17.428
and being part of the team was enough

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.261
just to get me to try.

00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:23.936
(smooth electronic music)

